r review: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101 (PR #101), with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. With HALF_UP, `2.665` rounds to `2.67` instead of `2.66`, so the test failed.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **Not merged:** Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy, so the PR is open for review and I did not merge it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the failing test and the module it exercises.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UqNxRfkg3QB59rw55UiZKV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UT98KcLkGaY525SvABL8BG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, but the code uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`. With HALF_UP, `2.665` rounds to `2.67` and the test fails. I'll create a branch and make the one-line fix there.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HdsiWaoTCg8avFwSMPbn4B", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013Sfyk8n8pd1Z52f4Hho3GD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Committed. Now I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KyacukE6yPKLg1U34R6fR2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-money-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Fu4ZtNMdiTmjPNPJBXEKVz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Er8kSUXgyA4UhFj4NxgmAv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` documented banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but was implemented with ROUND_HALF_UP. This changes the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN so the implementation matches the docstring and the test expectations:\n\n- round_money(2.675) -> 2.68 (unchanged)\n- round_money(2.665) -> 2.66 (previously 2.67)\n\nCI on fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212 (run ci-0001) passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-money-rounding-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in a pull request for review: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101 (PR #101), with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. With HALF_UP, `2.665` rounds to `2.67` instead of `2.66`, so the test failed.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **Not merged:** Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy, so the PR is open for review and I did not merge it.", "type": "text"}]}]}